{number: 80}
{title: Onward, Christian Soldiers}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Onward, Christian soldiers, marching as to [G7] war,
With the cross of [C] Jesus going on be-[G7] fore.
[C] Christ, the royal Master, leads a-[F] gainst the [C] foe;
Forward into [F] battle [C] see His [G7] banners [C] go!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Onward, Christian soldiers, marching as to [G7] war,
With the cross of [C] Jesus [F] going [C] on [G7] be-[C] fore.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] At the sign of triumph Satan's host doth [G7] flee;
On, then, Christian [C] soldiers, on to victo-[G7] ry!
[C] Hell's foundations quiver at the [F] shout of [C] praise;
Brothers, lift your [F] voices, [C] loud your [G7] anthems [C] raise!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Like a mighty army moves the Church of [G7] God;
Brothers, we are [C] treading where the saints have [G7] trod.
[C] We are not divided; all one [F] body [C] we,
One in hope and [F] doctrine, [C] one in [G7] chari-[C] ty.
{end_of_verse}
